# Host-side Python (Python 3.12, via uv): the no-JVM engines of the `light` profile, the no-Docker
# churn path and the T0-T3 test tiers. Spark jobs run inside ldl-spark and never use this file.
#
# Lock (hashes for every platform; constrained by the graph lock so pandas / numpy / pyarrow /
# pytest are the exact versions the graph venv and the parity checks use):
#   uv pip compile --universal --generate-hashes --python-version 3.12 \
#     -c requirements-graph.txt requirements.in -o requirements.txt
# Install (hash-checked):
#   make venv        # uv venv --python 3.12 .venv + uv pip sync --require-hashes requirements.txt
#   pip install --require-hashes -r requirements.txt     # CI
#
# Every dependency is open source (OSI).

# pandas gold twin (scripts/build_churn_gold_local.py) + sample generator. BSD-3-Clause.
